# CANONICAL §7.3 fixture — CircularPattern V2 body LINEAGE.
#
# `resultPolicyVersion: 2` is normative for Pattern: the SOURCE is instance zero and
# emits NO lifecycle event, and a non-fused pattern creates exactly `count-1`
# children named `body_<opId>:<k>`, where child k is transformed instance k+1. That
# naming is identity — a repair, a re-edit or a count reduction addresses children by
# it — so it belongs in the cross-track contract, not only in a C++ unit test.
#
# 20x20 rect extruded 25 (body_op1), then patterned 180 degrees in 3 instances about
# a Z-axis 100mm away, so the copies are far apart and no boolean can be implied.
#
# What this fixture deliberately does NOT pin: the per-instance step angle. The
# `angleDeg / count` rule (SCHEMA 7.3 — divides by count, NOT count-1) is a
# GEOMETRIC fact, and an NDJSON exchange carries no geometry to measure it with.
# It stays pinned where it is measurable: worker/tests/test_m6a_ops.cpp
# (test_circular_pattern_partial_sweep, successive polar deltas of exactly 60 deg)
# and src/tools/preview/patternPreview.test.ts on the frontend side. Asserting it
# here by proxy would be a test that cannot fail.
